MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The latest HD Fire TV Stick feels useful because it could add streaming to my older Samsung TV, provided its connections are compatible.",
    "The Fire HD 10 offers a meaningful change from my Fire 7: a larger screen for viewing photos and videos, with memory-card support something I would check before choosing it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older 7-inch Fire tablet repeats what I already have without a clear improvement, and the previous-generation streaming stick is less appealing than the latest HD option shown.",
    "The 4K stick's resolution does not offer a clear benefit for my 720p TV. Smart speakers, a smart plug, a portable speaker, and a Wi-Fi extender also lack a specific current need in my history."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning a Fire tablet seems to have been taken as interest in many Amazon and Alexa devices, although my purchases do not show a desire for voice control or home automation.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in more gadgets, when I usually choose accessories that serve a particular device or task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of memory cards, tripods, a card reader, and a lens cap suggest ongoing camera and storage needs that these recommendations barely address.",
    "Compatibility and a concrete improvement matter to me: cables must fit my devices, accessories must support my setup, and a replacement tablet needs to offer more than the one I own."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my tablet and TV interests but stretched them into general gadget interest instead of focusing on practical additions and meaningful upgrades."
}
